  "conclusion": "Bounded batch completion removes the observed sustained threshold slow segments on both A0 and B4 in this long diagnostic. The first 300 frames of one A0/B8 run remain transient; shared GPU warmup calibration and a fresh baseline are still required.",
  "nextStep": "Version the common bounded GPU sampling protocol, independently calibrate and freeze a shared GPU warmup across both variants and cases, then collect a fresh three-cohort baseline under the original 5% regression, 20% spread and 10% CV budgets.",
  "limits": [
    "All data are retained; 1.2 ms main-pass and 0.4 ms output thresholds describe diagnostics only.",
    "Both arms use whole-batch submit-to-fence bounds; external overlap is not per-frame attribution.",
    "B8 has 99-100 seconds of exposure versus 510-516 seconds for S8; this is not indefinite stability proof.",
    "Power states are observed, not locked; this experiment does not isolate a single driver-internal mechanism.",
    "The changed sampling synchronization needs its own common calibration and fresh acceptance population; diagnostic results are not a baseline."
  ],
